Unlike planar NAND, which stores memory cells across a two-dimensional surface, 3D NAND stacks memory cells vertically across multiple layers. This architecture enables manufacturers to increase storage density without relying exclusively on further reductions in cell dimensions. Higher layer counts, improvements in manufacturing processes and growing demand for high-capacity solid-state storage are strengthening the technology's role in the semiconductor memory ecosystem.

